 ],
 "summary": "Liver. Fructose skips PFK-1 (the main glycolytic control point), so it enters glycolysis faster and unregulated. Two disorders: essential fructosuria (fructokinase, benign) and hereditary fructose intolerance (aldolase B, dangerous).",
